enance work that you have onboard  the vessels today and then on the  efficiency side you can of course now  have the same team of experts sitting in  a in a good office environment  supporting multiple ships or tens of  ships instead of having technical  expertise in in each of the ships so the  work is the same but now more more  efficient  we can already use a lot of solutions  that have been created for other  industries in the machine learning space  and we can now apply them to change the  shipping world as well there's a lot of  things we haven't done yet so we need to  for example create you know the machine  learning models and train them for for  marine use we need to basically gather  the data so that we can we can train the  models also for example in night time  and so it and different weather  conditions and different viewing angles  that kind of data set we need to create  so we can have the best models out there  in in in ships you have a wider area to  cover and we're using lidar using radar  HD cameras they have to cover so much  white area because there can be very  unpredictable of a lot of vessels that  requires a high computing power onboard  the vessel and the good thing is that  they have a bit more time to do the  analysis for example compared to cars  some of the Google cloud technologies  were using include for example  tensorflow processing unit that we can  have on onboard the vessels you have  data jobs you have hyper tune and and in  data labs those are the the tools that  have solutions that have immediate  benefit for for the autonomous ships key  takeaway is basically speed and  flexibility to bring this to the market  fast so don't try to do too many things  in-house partner use open platforms and  collaboration to drive this innovation  fast

